course: dictionary
lesson: 4573
title: Helium: the light gas
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Helium is a very light gas. It has no colour and no smell, so you cannot see or smell it. It is lighter than air, which is why a helium balloon floats up. «The party balloons were filled with helium.»
explain: Helium is also a chemical element, a basic kind of stuff that cannot be split into anything simpler. Its symbol is He. It is the second lightest element of all, after hydrogen.
explain: Helium does not burn, so it is safer than hydrogen in airships. But you must never breathe it in from balloons or tanks. It can stop your body getting oxygen and make you pass out.
fact: Helium is a very light gas with no colour and no smell.
fact: Helium is lighter than air, so helium balloons rise.
fact: Helium is a chemical element with the symbol He.
fact: Helium is the second lightest of all the elements.
fact: Deep in the Sun's core, hydrogen is squeezed into helium, giving out enormous energy.
exercise: «The party balloons were filled with helium.» Why do helium balloons rise? | *Helium is lighter than air | Helium is hot like the Sun | Helium is heavier than air | Helium is painted on the rubber
exercise: What is the chemical symbol for helium? | H | *He | Hl | Hm
exercise: Why is helium safer than hydrogen in airships? | It has a strong smell | *It does not burn | It is heavier than air | Helium is made in tanks
test: Which statement about helium is true? | It has a strong smell like a gas leak | It is a heavy liquid that sinks | *It is a very light gas with no colour or smell | It is a metal that you can see
test: Why must you never breathe in helium from a balloon? | It tastes bitter | It makes your hair grow | It turns your skin blue | *It can stop your body getting oxygen and make you pass out
exam: The Sun makes helium from which gas? | Oxygen | Iron | *Hydrogen | Nitrogen
